title: Running only the tests a change can touch would save little.
pid: 822d7c17-1ba6-4148-ab2f-ad670343da35
body: |2-
  The Rust tests themselves run in 16 to 47 s; what costs is compiling
  them, 35 s after an edit, and choosing tests does not avoid that. A
  change only to an editor client's code can already run that client's
  tests alone.
